# The WebKit revision Quickie's engine is built from. One KEY=value per line, POSIX sh syntax:
# engine/webkit/scripts/sync and .github/workflows/webkit.yml read this file, nothing else does.
#
# WEBKIT_REPO     our fork of WebKit/WebKit; our patches will be commits on a branch there
# WEBKIT_BRANCH   the fork branch the commit is taken from (informational: sync fetches the commit
#                 and prints where the branch is now, so a stale pin is visible)
# WEBKIT_COMMIT   the exact commit that is fetched and built; the only value the build trusts
# WEBKIT_CHECKED  when WEBKIT_COMMIT was read off WEBKIT_BRANCH (UTC date)
#
# Base: the WebKitGTK/WPE stable series, the one branch both ports (macOS and GTK) build from
# (docs/architecture.md, "Decision: our own WebKit"). Release tag webkitgtk-2.54.3
# (tagged 2026-11-18) peels to eb74cd57; the fork's branch quickie/2.54 starts there and will
# carry our patches as commits. The first two are Cocoa-only build fixes for code the GTK/WPE
# ports never compile: 02fa3f47 (WebPageProxy::transcodeChosenFiles) and c6ffa6ac
# (PlatformPasteboard::isFilePasteboardType, used by a cherry-picked drag check). Apple's Mac-only security fixes are
# cherry-picked from each Apple security note; the series moves to webkitglib/2.56 when released.
#
# To bump: put the new commit and date here, push, and let .github/workflows/webkit.yml build it
# (engine/README.md, "Bumping the pin").

WEBKIT_REPO=https://github.com/izevg/WebKit.git
WEBKIT_BRANCH=quickie/2.54
WEBKIT_COMMIT=c6ffa6acfc40316ba683afb0272233e6921eb09b
WEBKIT_CHECKED=2026-11-20
